{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q420409","formula":"C₁₃H₂₀O","hill":"C13H20O","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":20.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Ionone","ru":"Ионон"},"descriptions":{"en":"The ionones, from greek ἴον ion \"violet\", are a series of closely related chemical substances that are part of a group of compounds known as rose ketones, which also includes damascones and damascenones. Ionones are aroma compounds found in a variety of essential oils, including rose oil. β-Ionone is a significant contributor to the aroma of roses, despite its relatively low concentration, and is an important fragrance chemical used in perfumery.","ru":"Иононы — изомеры, ненасыщенные кетоны из группы оксоалкенилзамещённых циклогексенов, обладающие приятным цветочным запахом. α-ионон — 1-(1,1,3-триметилциклогекс-3-ен-2-ил)бут-1-ен-3-он. β-ионон — 1-(1,1,3-триметилциклогекс-2-ен-2-ил)бут-1-ен-3-он."},"fame":29,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q15711994","names":{"en":"group of isomeric entities","ru":"семейство химических соединений","uk":"родина хімічних сполук"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420409","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%98%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q422740","formula":"C₁₂H₁₈O","names":{"en":"Propofol","ru":"Пропофол","uk":"Пропофол"},"elements":["H","C","O"],"fame":56,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q321285","formula":"C₅₉H₉₀O₄","names":{"en":"Ubidecarenone","ru":"Кофермент Q","uk":"Убіхінон"},"elements":["H","C","O"],"fame":41,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q1946346","formula":"C₁₂H₁₈O","names":{"en":"Amylmetacresol"},"elements":["H","C","O"],"fame":13,"kind":"molec